l had been fourth after round one with 12 faults, and matched that number in the second round to move up to third, as France recorded 16 faults to drop off the podium. Brazil had also won a bronze medal in this event 1996, its only two equestrian medals to this date. German " [:a {:href "/athletes/11606"} "Ludger Beerbaum"] " won his fourth consecutive gold medal, winning the individual in 1992, and with the team in 1988, 1996, and 2000, although in Sydney, his score was not used in either round."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Faults"] [:th {} "Jump-Off Faults"] [:th {} "Jump-Off Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Germany"] [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "15.00"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "247"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11603"} "Otto Becker"] " "] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/431"} "Cento"]]] [:td {}] [:td {} "0.00"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "249"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/90696"} "Marcus Ehning"] " "] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/912"} "For Pleasure"]]] [:td {}] [:td {} "7.00"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "252"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12492"} "Lars Nieberg"] " "] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/803"} "Esprit FRH"]]] [:td {}] [:td {} "8.00"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "250"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/ath